{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.residue_nontrivial_of_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.residue_nontrivial_of_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L181-L186","doc":"The Brunnian residue space is nontrivial — the exact opposite of the\nHopf-spectator collapse: the open gate carries information. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.residue_eq_int_of_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.residue_eq_int_of_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L176-L179","doc":"The residue space of a Brunnian (pure-α) triple is the integers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.intCast_injective_of_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.intCast_injective_of_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L162-L174","doc":"**Audit corollary, Brunnian side.**  For a pure-α triple (all pairwise\nlinkings zero) the integer content of μ̄ is fully preserved: the cast\n`ℤ → Residue = ZMod 0` is injective, so distinct integer values of\nμ̄(ijs) stay distinct — the α-only gate is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.intCast_residue_collapse_of_hopfSpectator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.intCast_residue_collapse_of_hopfSpectator","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L154-L160","doc":"Restatement on integer representatives: with a Hopf-linked pair present,\nany two integer values of μ̄ have the same residue — no invariant triple\ncontent survives the indeterminacy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.residue_trivial_of_hopfSpectator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.residue_trivial_of_hopfSpectator","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L144-L152","doc":"**Audit corollary, Hopf side.**  In a cluster arrangement where a light\nspectator is Hopf-linked into the triple, the triple channel is trivial:\nALL residues of μ̄(ijs) coincide — in particular every two integer\ncandidate values of μ̄ become equal in the residue space, so the triple\ninvariant distinguishes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.Brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.Brunnian","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L135-L142","doc":"All pairwise linkings vanish: the Brunnian/Borromean pattern\n(a pure-α triple).\n\n**This is TIER 2 — strictly weaker than true Brunnian-ness** (every proper\nsub-link is the unlink), which it does not imply: the Whitehead link has\nlinking number `0` and is not the unlink.  Tier table for the four things this corpus calls `Brunnian`, and which implications hold: `QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.HopfSpectator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.HopfSpectator","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L130-L133","doc":"The triple contains a Hopf-linked pair (`|lk| = 1`): the audit's\nlight-spectator configuration (n/d/t pairwise Hopf-linked to an α). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.Residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.Residue","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L126-L128","doc":"The residue space in which μ̄(ijs) is well-defined (Milnor 1954).\n`abbrev` so that the `ZMod` ring instances are found on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.indeterminacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.indeterminacy","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L122-L124","doc":"The Milnor indeterminacy of the triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.l23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.l23","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L118-L118","doc":"Pairwise linking number of components j, s. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.l13","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.l13","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Pairwise linking number of components i, s. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.l12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.l12","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Pairwise linking number of components i, j. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.ClusterTriple","kind":"structure","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L105-L118","doc":"A 3-component sub-link of a cluster arrangement, carried abstractly by\nits pairwise linking data `l12 = lk(i,j)`, `l13 = lk(i,s)`,\n`l23 = lk(j,s)`.  Modeling input (Milnor 1954, carried here as the type\nof the residue, not as an axiom): the triple invariant μ̄(ijs) of the\nsub-link is a well-defined element of `ZMod (indeterminacy l12 l13 l23)`\nonly — any integer representative is meaningful only through its residue\nclass modulo the gcd of the pairwise linkings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.residue_eq_int_of_zero_linkings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.residue_eq_int_of_zero_linkings","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L95-L101","doc":"In the Brunnian case the residue space IS the integers:\n`ZMod Δ = ZMod 0 = ℤ` (definitional once the gcd is rewritten to 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.gate_open_iff_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.gate_open_iff_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Gate open iff Brunnian (audit I3(b)).**  The indeterminacy vanishes —\nequivalently, the residue space is `ZMod 0 = ℤ`, full integer μ̄\ncontent — iff ALL pairwise linking numbers vanish: the\nBrunnian/Borromean pattern. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:alpha-cluster-activation-gate","label":"prop:alpha-cluster-activation-gate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-cluster-activation-gate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.gate_kills_hopf_spectator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.gate_kills_hopf_spectator","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**Gate kills the Hopf spectator (audit I3(a)).**  If any pair in the\ntriple is Hopf-linked (`|lk| = 1` — the always-on light-spectator\nchannel), the Milnor residue space `ZMod Δ(ijs) = ZMod 1` is a\nsubsingleton: the residue class of μ̄(ijs) is trivial and carries no\ninvariant triple content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.indeterminacy_eq_one_of_unit_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.indeterminacy_eq_one_of_unit_pair","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L64-L70","doc":"If any pair of the triple has `|lk| = 1` (a Hopf-linked pair), the\nindeterminacy is total: `Δ(ijs) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.indeterminacy_eq_int_gcd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.indeterminacy_eq_int_gcd","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L59-L62","doc":"The natAbs-gcd of the definition agrees with the iterated `Int.gcd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.indeterminacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate.indeterminacy","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorIndeterminacyGate.lean#L49-L57","doc":"The Milnor indeterminacy `Δ(ijs)` of a 3-component sub-link with pairwise\nlinking numbers `l12, l13, l23`: the gcd of the three pairwise linking\nnumbers.  Milnor 1954: μ̄(ijs) is a well-defined residue only modulo this\ngcd (the lower-order invariants of the proper sub-links of a 3-component\nlink are exactly the pairwise linking numbers).  Computed on `ℤ.natAbs`\nsince the gcd of integers is a natural number and `ZMod` is indexed by\n`ℕ`; this agrees with `Int.gcd`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}